# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
# This repo's tooling assumes LF: nx's pnpm-lock.yaml document splitter matches
# on "---\n" exactly, and the .sh build scripts are run through bash. A CRLF
# checkout (e.g. from core.autocrlf=true on Windows) breaks both.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are stored byte-for-byte as committed (most of the vendored
# gradlew.bat files already have CRLF blobs). `-text` disables conversion in
# both directions -- `text eol=crlf` would instead rewrite those blobs to LF on
# the next `git add`, silently changing files nothing here needs changed.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text

# Explicitly binary: never touched by line-ending conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.jar binary
*.wasm binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary

docs/** linguist-documentation
website/** linguist-documentation

